{
  "_comment": [
    "THE permission catalog: the single declaration of which permission codes exist",
    "at all, plus the built-in role templates seeded into every tenant.",
    "",
    "This file is the SOURCE. The Go and Python constant tables next to it are",
    "GENERATED from it by scripts/gen-rbac-catalog.py; both languages also assert",
    "their generated table against this file, so a drift fails the test suites",
    "instead of surfacing in production as a permission nobody can ever hold.",
    "",
    "Relationship to the database: identity-service synchronizes this catalog into",
    "the `permissions` table on startup (Store.SyncPermissions). The table is a",
    "projection used to render the role editor and to keep historical role",
    "compositions readable after a code is retired; it is never a source of truth",
    "and is never written through the API, so a permission code cannot be invented",
    "by writing to the database. ROLE COMPOSITION (roles / role_permissions) is",
    "the opposite: the database owns it and tenants may edit it, including for the",
    "built-in roles.",
    "",
    "Adding a permission point = adding an entry here + regenerating. Adding it to",
    "a role template also backfills tenants whose built-in role is un-customized",
    "(Store.EnsureTenantRoles); customized roles are reported as drift instead."
  ],
